From cb3f719cc7a7b35ff2d4f7af069393749e4d8f4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:25:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(js): checkVisibility, selectedOptions, option.label,
 readOnly, isContentEditable

checkVisibility() returned true for every element, so display:none,
visibility:hidden and opacity:0 content read as visible. It now follows
CSSOM View from layout: no box is false; checkVisibilityCSS rejects a
hidden computed visibility (inherited); checkOpacity rejects opacity 0 on
the element or an ancestor.

<select>.selectedOptions was missing (spreading it threw),
<option>.label, <input>/<textarea>.readOnly and isContentEditable were
undefined. Setting label, readOnly or selectedOptions on an element they
do not apply to keeps a plain property, as before.
---
